# A green full verification and a green scoped verification each write their
# record at the asking root, and neither changes what a push owes.
#
# The fixture builds a throwaway Ze checkout with a bare upstream, commits one
# change, and asserts the REAL `le commit debt-status` exits 0: a push owes no
# verify. It then runs verify.Run, the lifecycle `le verify worktree` answers
# through, with a fixture action runner that answers every stage green: a
# native run over the real population takes this machine's job slots for most
# of an hour. It asserts the green record sits at the asking root naming HEAD,
# uncut. It runs verify.Run over the changed population, the lifecycle
# `le verify changed` answers through, with the same fixture action runner,
# asserts the scoped record at the asking root names HEAD, and that
# `le commit debt-status` still exits 0.
#
# Spec: spec-verification-debt-derived (closed; design in docs/architecture/testing/verify-freshness-scope.md) (AC-8).
# Delete the green-record write from the lifecycle (internal/le/verify/lifecycle.go)
# and seq=1 fails at green-record-at-asking-root; delete the scoped-record
# write (recordChanged, internal/le/verify/changed.go) and seq=1 fails at
# scoped-record-at-asking-root.

option=timeout:value=120s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture runner/verify-records-at-asking-root
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=push-owes-no-verify
expect=stdout:contains=green-record-at-asking-root
expect=stdout:contains=scoped-record-at-asking-root
expect=stdout:contains=push-still-owes-no-verify
